21b5cca9-74d6-4999-9b31-fdb8cd9d9eb4	e1811769-e50e-4b03-be07-16f0057b5749	12	Class 12 - Integration: Sums That Never End	multi_section	\N	\N	Integration is the opposite of differentiation. It helps us find the total area under a curve. The simplest rule: the integral of x^n is x^(n+1)/(n+1) (when n is not -1). For example, the integral of x is x^2/2 + C, where C is a constant we add.	e981b3ae-06da-4212-a4e0-aba08e0f2773	2026-05-30 23:51:28.357728	2026-05-30 23:51:28.357728	f	2c0392cc-0263-41a8-9dd0-7d4c35960f8e
cc0096d6-cf09-4b00-9487-292324c907d5	e1811769-e50e-4b03-be07-16f0057b5749	12	Class 12 - Wave Optics: Light as a Wave	multi_section	\N	\N	Light behaves like a wave. Two waves can meet and add up (constructive) or cancel out (destructive) - this is called interference. We can see colourful patterns in soap bubbles because of interference.	e981b3ae-06da-4212-a4e0-aba08e0f2773	2026-05-30 23:51:28.496095	2026-05-30 23:51:28.496095	f	653d2348-553b-4d62-8825-1fed78b261ae
4caa684b-be8d-40ce-8623-13e86119aead	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	1	Numbers 1 to 20	multi_section	\N	\N	In this lesson we count from 1 up to 20. We learn to say each number, write it, and count small groups of objects.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:35.299659	2026-05-31 00:16:35.299659	f	3afa10fd-084f-4301-bb74-90b189e3128e
edec7c75-f4aa-476d-bc53-a539becfe8f4	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	1	Naming Words (Nouns)	multi_section	\N	\N	A naming word, or noun, is the name of a person, place, animal, or thing. "Dog", "Ravi", "school", and "ball" are all naming words.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:35.453528	2026-05-31 00:16:35.453528	f	efa0f5a7-735c-42cd-ba67-cc70ffedb4fc
8912d09c-99df-4183-9df3-5e98e386ac12	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	2	Addition up to 100	multi_section	\N	\N	When we add two numbers we put them together and count the total. 23 + 14 = 37. We can add tens with tens and ones with ones.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:36.67951	2026-05-31 00:16:36.67951	f	c2e10612-558d-4f7b-978c-fb2abdf7d1f4
39c6f649-78aa-4b2a-b3e0-a8a79de89a42	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	2	Action Words (Verbs)	multi_section	\N	\N	An action word, or verb, tells what someone or something is doing. "Jump", "read", "sing", and "play" are action words.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:36.800534	2026-05-31 00:16:36.800534	f	61f7c109-8530-4d31-b7f1-399d708e5ed9
d2e22931-34a7-49e4-8aa2-034508b7c7f1	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	4	Multiplication and Times Tables	multi_section	\N	\N	Multiplication is repeated addition. 4 × 3 means 4 added 3 times = 12. Times tables help us multiply quickly.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:37.858925	2026-05-31 00:16:37.858925	f	cd517f2c-9be4-4ee9-bd90-be07a128a6af
b61cfa46-25a1-4016-aac4-55685785a2bf	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	4	Parts of a Plant	multi_section	\N	\N	A plant has four main parts: roots (hold the plant and absorb water), stem (carries water and food), leaves (make food using sunlight), and flowers (which become fruits and seeds).	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:37.952161	2026-05-31 00:16:37.952161	f	6cfba8ae-9bd0-4eb5-8b69-2b79f82eb164
cead3e22-b2d9-4f2b-a80d-ab8b4dc231ca	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	5	Fractions and Decimals	multi_section	\N	\N	A fraction shows part of a whole, like 1/2 or 3/4. A decimal also shows part of a whole using a point: 0.5 = 1/2, 0.25 = 1/4.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:38.96603	2026-05-31 00:16:38.96603	f	4254ab39-55a9-4e87-af2e-7961ed880f4f
b358e5b5-df72-4571-921e-0baa33784146	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	5	Our Body and Its Systems	multi_section	\N	\N	The human body has systems that work together: the skeletal system gives shape, the muscular system helps us move, the digestive system breaks down food, and the respiratory system helps us breathe.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:39.079486	2026-05-31 00:16:39.079486	f	a522f0b8-d2cf-4e65-97d2-ee84f3bd6bf0
67d0b1f3-131b-42ad-a121-0af04a017422	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	6	Whole Numbers and Integers	multi_section	\N	\N	Whole numbers are 0, 1, 2, 3, ... Integers include negative numbers, zero, and positive numbers (..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ...). Adding a positive moves right, adding a negative moves left on the number line.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:40.170544	2026-05-31 00:16:40.170544	f	71416f26-dc28-4a4a-89b9-671e8cac431c
9977a96c-2a91-46cd-8584-c80d87f55f07	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	6	Components of Food	multi_section	\N	\N	Food contains nutrients we need: carbohydrates (energy), proteins (growth and repair), fats (energy storage), vitamins and minerals (good health), and water (every body process).	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:40.300612	2026-05-31 00:16:40.300612	f	79e3da32-c7e6-4643-b681-573193fa89f9
d55adf31-8949-43a9-adcc-1ca2968a84d9	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	8	Linear Equations in One Variable	multi_section	\N	\N	A linear equation in one variable looks like ax + b = c. We solve it by isolating x: bring all x terms to one side and constants to the other, then divide by the coefficient of x.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:41.37036	2026-05-31 00:16:41.37036	f	cc4f0635-3ac5-43bb-a93f-8707da071e35
d1cc47d0-0cac-4707-bfc9-b6d3f4175a32	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	8	Force and Pressure	multi_section	\N	\N	Force is a push or pull. Pressure is force divided by the area it acts on (P = F/A). The same force on a smaller area gives more pressure - that is why a sharp knife cuts more easily than a blunt one.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:41.477505	2026-05-31 00:16:41.477505	f	eb62a1c9-cadf-4ce9-8f43-90a721f18136
520df216-5f42-42d2-8084-bf5b06a20656	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	9	Polynomials	multi_section	\N	\N	A polynomial is an expression of the form a_n x^n + ... + a_1 x + a_0 with whole-number powers of x. The degree is the highest power. A linear polynomial has degree 1, quadratic 2, cubic 3.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:42.623699	2026-05-31 00:16:42.623699	f	dffe87a3-85fa-4aae-a8a1-ceb79e2d3ac3
7c2cca82-d7a6-46c9-82f2-1b9e40398f03	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	9	Atoms and Molecules	multi_section	\N	\N	All matter is made of atoms. An atom has a tiny nucleus of protons and neutrons, surrounded by electrons. A molecule is two or more atoms bonded together (e.g. H2O has 2 hydrogens + 1 oxygen).	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:42.755503	2026-05-31 00:16:42.755503	f	94af1626-5828-4bd9-9a5a-e52c91ec52f9
9daabd2d-b6a9-4ee6-bfda-8592d0defb86	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	10	Quadratic Equations	multi_section	\N	\N	A quadratic equation has the form ax^2 + bx + c = 0 with a != 0. It can be solved by factorisation, completing the square, or the quadratic formula x = (-b +- sqrt(b^2 - 4ac)) / 2a.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:43.819633	2026-05-31 00:16:43.819633	f	7b054446-c922-4f2c-ad50-3fd763b486b4
d074d96b-01da-4601-9128-c490ff07a0d9	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	10	Acids, Bases and Salts	multi_section	\N	\N	Acids release H+ ions in water (e.g. HCl, H2SO4) and turn blue litmus red. Bases release OH- ions (e.g. NaOH, KOH) and turn red litmus blue. Acid + base -> salt + water.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:43.943646	2026-05-31 00:16:43.943646	f	2ff4b32a-7723-422d-a24f-e55df5e608ec
0871c592-e9af-4e48-8a6c-a7286f08cd03	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	11	Sets and Functions	multi_section	\N	\N	A set is a well-defined collection of objects. Operations include union (A U B), intersection (A n B), and difference (A - B). A function f: A -> B assigns to each element of A exactly one element of B.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:45.005253	2026-05-31 00:16:45.005253	f	5194ebb4-8b5c-4f05-bdba-b5e4537968ae
e9f9b930-280c-4da9-8241-f96387f9a977	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	11	Kinematics: Motion in a Straight Line	multi_section	\N	\N	Kinematics describes motion using displacement, velocity, and acceleration. For uniform acceleration: v = u + at, s = ut + (1/2) a t^2, v^2 = u^2 + 2 a s.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:45.117541	2026-05-31 00:16:45.117541	f	fb36ae14-6b07-48fa-8c73-a7506bde9926
9566d083-0851-4082-98e1-336dd5b25f1c	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	12	Calculus: Differentiation	multi_section	\N	\N	The derivative of f(x) at x measures the instantaneous rate of change. Standard rules: d/dx(x^n) = n x^(n-1), d/dx(sin x) = cos x, d/dx(e^x) = e^x. Product, quotient and chain rules combine these for complex functions.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:46.149726	2026-05-31 00:16:46.149726	f	b4385065-6ad0-4f0c-b7fa-9506539b504a
dffef31d-f139-4545-a599-264ba0e494f6	8ba8388f-9907-486c-9883-3784c2f2f34e	12	Electromagnetic Induction	multi_section	\N	\N	Faraday's law: a changing magnetic flux through a coil induces an EMF in the coil. EMF = -dPhi/dt. Lenz's law fixes the sign so the induced current opposes the change in flux. This principle drives generators and transformers.	2bb3d34c-4eae-46bd-8f24-cf1c9096ac70	2026-05-31 00:16:46.250541	2026-05-31 00:16:46.250541	f	3b697807-e6ca-4485-9e76-4c3347b1f286
